From 5b8cab3e0a89515066e8c11ca2460d1661992382 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ObeseCatLord <6099645+ObeseCatLord@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 22:17:59 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 179/180] Native 3D, desktop M1: the battle map drawn natively
 under the game's 2D

- ga2_native3d: the per-frame capture (the game camera as VU1 applies it, the battle's units), published by the game
  thread with the guest flip that shows it; the GS frames now carry that flip to the presenter (slot -> eye ->
  SharedFrame / takeEyeFrame / ga2_zerocopy::take), so each picture pairs with its own camera.
- ga2_nativemap (GL, the presenter): identifies the stage from the units (battlevr), draws the stage's sky (view
  rotation, brightness 0.55 as measured against the game's picture) and map model (identity world matrix, map units)
  with the game's projection (x = cx + scrz*ax*X/Z on the 640-wide window; the frame's 448 rows show 480 game rows),
  lays the game's remaining 3D (effects) over it keyed by brightness, and the 2D from the UI layer instance with its
  alpha. Split frames outside the map get the UI layer over the scene. GA2_NATIVE_MAP=0 off; GA2_NATIVE_MAP_DEBUG=1
  draws the native lines in magenta over the game's own map (registration check: they coincide).
- gs_pgs: the UI layer instance also runs on the desktop when the native map is on (its work is on the GS worker:
  no game-thread cost measured), split while the native map is ready.

The game skips its map meshes meanwhile (native/compat/ga2_battledraw.cpp). Eigou 1 battle on the RTX 4090 path at a
144 cap: 144 iterations/s at full speed, governor load ~0.8 (the game drew it: 60-75).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
